You can have a class for the Dialogue, which contains the text and the options. Then each option can have a reference to the next Dialogue (or a function to call, etc). Then you can have a loop that displays the current dialogue, and then processes the user input to choose the next dialogue.
For example:
public class Dialogue {
    private String text;
    private List<Choice> choices;

    public Dialogue(String text, List<Choice> choices) {
        this.text = text;
        this.choices = choices;
    }

    public void display() {
        System.out.println(text);
        for (int i = 0; i < choices.size(); i++) {
            System.out.println((i + 1) + ". " + choices.get(i).getText());
        }
    }

    public Dialogue processInput(int choice) {
        return choices.get(choice - 1).getNextDialogue();
    }
}

public class Choice {
    private String text;
    private Dialogue nextDialogue;

    public Choice(String text, Dialogue nextDialogue) {
        this.text = text;
        this.nextDialogue = nextDialogue;
    }

    public String getText() {
        return text;
    }

    public Dialogue getNextDialogue() {
        return nextDialogue;
    }
}
